### Problem

On the interpreter booth page, the mic handover button (**PASS MIC** / **TAKE OVER**) changes colour to show where a handover stands:

| State | Colour | Text |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Idle | white | dark |
| You started a handover | green | white |
| Your boothmate offered or asked | flashing yellow | dark |

When the mouse is over the green or flashing button, the label turns **blue** and the border changes. Blue on green is hard to read. That happens exactly when the interpreter points at the button to cancel or accept a handover, which is the moment they need to read it.

![Handover button states with three interpreters](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ArnavBallinCode/voxbento/pr-assets-757/issues/handover-hover-contrast.png)

The screenshot is from a local run with three interpreters in one booth. The buttons that were just clicked still have the mouse over them: Ana's green **PASS MIC**, Ben's green **TAKE OVER** and Cara's flashing **PASS MIC** all show blue text.

### Cause

In `portal/static/css/interpreter.css`, the generic hover rule

```css
.header-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
  border-color: var(--bx-accent);
  color: var(--bx-accent-ink);
  ...
}
```

is more specific (one class plus two pseudo-classes) than the handover state rules `.header-btn--handover.state-green` and `.header-btn--handover.state-flash-yellow` (two classes). So on hover it replaces their text and border colour. The mic button avoids this with its own `:hover` rules (`.header-btn--mic.muted:hover`, `.header-btn--mic.unmuted:hover`); the handover button has none.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Open the same booth as two interpreters (two browsers or profiles).
2. As the live interpreter, press **PASS MIC**. It turns green and the other interpreter's **TAKE OVER** flashes yellow.
3. Move the mouse over either button: the label turns blue.

### Expected

Hovering keeps the state colours (white text on green, dark text on yellow), with at most a slightly darker background as the hover cue, like the mic button.

### Suggested fix

Add hover rules for the two coloured handover states in `portal/static/css/interpreter.css`, for example:

```css
.header-btn--handover.state-green:hover:not(:disabled) {
  background: var(--bx-live-ink);
  color: #fff;
  border-color: var(--bx-live-ink);
}

.header-btn--handover.state-flash-yellow:hover:not(:disabled) {
  color: #1c1e21;
  border-color: #d97706;
}
```

Check the result at normal and high zoom, and that keyboard focus is still visible.

### Not affected

The handover logic itself works. Offer, request, cancel and accept, simultaneous **TAKE OVER** presses, and the live interpreter leaving were checked end to end with three interpreters (24/24 repeated handovers switched correctly). This issue is only about the colours on hover.

