## Summary

No CSS file in the project defines `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` rules. Yet the error pages (404, 500) already use dark backgrounds (`bg-gray-900`), and the listener captions box uses a dark background (`#222`). Users with system dark mode preferences see a jarring mix of light and dark pages.

## Evidence

- No `prefers-color-scheme` media queries in `admin.css`, `interpreter.css`, or `landing.css`
- 404/500 pages use dark backgrounds (Tailwind `bg-gray-900`)
- Listener captions box uses `background: #222`
- Home page uses `bg-slate-50` (light)

## Proposed Approach

1. Define dark-mode variants of CSS custom properties in a `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` block
2. Start with the admin panel and error pages (simplest palettes)
3. Extend to interpreter booth and listener pages

Example:
```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --color-bg: #1a1a2e;
    --color-surface: #16213e;
    --color-text: #e0e0e0;
    --color-border: #2a2a4a;
    /* ... */
  }
}
```

## Effort
Large — adding dark mode across a multi-stylesheet project is significant. Can be done incrementally.

